<section class="en-section en-concrete"><div class="wrap en-split">
  <div><span class="en-label">Swiss insurance, explained</span><h2>Know what your policy covers.</h2><p class="en-intro">Before booking, ask your insurer about the named practitioner, proposed treatment and your specific policy.</p><a class="tcm-btn tcm-btn--mint" href="/en/health-insurance-acupuncture/">Insurance & costs →</a></div>
  <div>
    <h3>Basic and supplementary cover</h3><p>Basic insurance can cover acupuncture provided by appropriately qualified physicians under its rules. Treatment by non-physician therapists falls outside that benefit; supplementary cover may contribute.</p>
    <h3>Recognition is part of the check</h3><p>EMR is a Swiss quality register for complementary-medicine practitioners. A registration alone does not guarantee that your insurer covers your treatment.</p>
    <h3>Ask about the full cost</h3><p>Confirm the consultation fee, likely follow-up costs, policy limits and billing procedure. Keep your itemised invoice and follow your insurer’s claim instructions.</p>
    <p class="en-note">Sources: <a href="https://www.bag.admin.ch/de/arztliche-komplementaermedizin">BAG (German)</a> · <a href="https://www.css.ch/en/private-customers/quick-easy/get-help/benefits-check/alternative-methods.html">CSS benefits guidance</a> · <a href="https://emr.ch/de/das-emr">EMR (German)</a></p>
  </div>
</div></section>
